## Component Documentation

### ContributionFlow
The main container component for the data contribution flow documentation.

### FlowSection
Represents a major section of the contribution flow.

Props:
- `title`: string - The section title
- `type`: 'process' | 'resources' | 'requirements' - The type of section
- `description`: string - A brief description of the section

### FlowStep
Represents a specific step in the contribution process.

Props:
- `step`: string - The step description
- `order`: number - The sequential order of the step
- `type`: 'preparation' | 'submission' | 'validation' | 'reward' | 'distribution' - The type of step
- `importance`: 'high' | 'medium' | 'low' - The importance level
- `description`: string - A brief description of the step
- `tool`: string - The tool used in this step
- `requirements`: string[] - Array of requirements for this step

### ToolSection
Represents a section of tools and resources.

Props:
- `title`: string - The section title
- `type`: 'resources' | 'development' | 'validation' - The type of section
- `description`: string - A brief description of the section

### ContributionTool
Represents a specific tool used in the contribution process.

Props:
- `tool`: string - The tool name
- `type`: 'development' | 'validation' | 'distribution' - The type of tool
- `importance`: 'high' | 'medium' | 'low' - The importance level
- `description`: string - A brief description of the tool
- `features`: string[] - Array of tool features

## Usage Example

```tsx
<ContributionFlow>
  <FlowSection
    title="Example Section"
    type="process"
    description="Example section description"
  >
    <FlowStep
      step="Example Step"
      order={1}
      type="preparation"
      importance="high"
      description="Example step description"
      tool="Example Tool"
      requirements={["Example requirement"]}
    />
  </FlowSection>
</ContributionFlow>
```

## Notes
- Each step must be completed in sequence
- All requirements must be met before proceeding
- Document any step-specific prerequisites
- Include error handling procedures
- Specify timeout and retry policies
- Document data format requirements
- Include privacy and security considerations
- Specify validation criteria for each step
